# Boundaries

Two folders, opposite rules. The canonical rules file is `AGENTS.md` at the repository root — read
it before non-trivial work. Each folder has its own `AGENTS.md` with local detail; the root file
wins on any disagreement.

- **`anatomy-explorer/` is the build target.** All new work goes here. Its `AGENTS.md` lists the
  current defects; its `PORT-CHECKLIST.md` lists what still needs bringing across and in what order.
- **`patient-library/` is live and reference-only.** It is deployed, a physiotherapist is entering
  clinical content into it, and patients have the link. **Read it and copy out of it. Never edit,
  refactor, reformat or delete anything in it.** It is not deprecated — it is the rollback target.
  If a task seems to require editing it, stop and ask.

## Copy code in; never import across the boundary

`anatomy-explorer/src/lib/library.ts` currently imports
`../../../patient-library/src/data/areas.json`. Do not add more of these and do not build on it.
It cannot deploy — Vercel with Root Directory `anatomy-explorer` never uploads files above that
folder — and it bypasses the Zod schemas, `validate.ts` and the compliance gate.

## Destructive git commands are unsafe here

Neither folder is committed; `git ls-files` returns zero for both, so there is no reflog to recover
from. **Never run `git clean -fd`, `git clean -fdx`, or `git checkout -- .` at the repository
root.** `git reset --hard` is survivable; `git clean` is not.

## Config changes are never a side effect

Do not modify `astro.config.mjs`, `package.json`, lockfiles, `tsconfig.json` or `.github/` while
doing something else. An agent deleted `astro.config.mjs` mid-task once and the Vercel adapter and
sitemap were missing for days. If a task genuinely needs a config change, say so and stop.
